{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 7: Mood Persistence (CharmNetwork Lite)",
  "description": "See how LSTM smooths mood transitions over time!\n\nWHY THIS MATTERS:\nMood doesn't jump instantly. If you're happy and something\nsad happens, you don't immediately become sad - there's\na transition period.\n\nTHIS IS THE CORE OF CHARMNETWORK!\nThe LSTM's hidden state carries 'emotional momentum':\n- Quick spikes get smoothed\n- Sustained input shifts mood gradually\n- Reset states = instant mood change (unrealistic!)\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Input high valence (happy) for several steps\n2. Watch affect visualization respond\n3. Switch to low valence (sad)\n4. Watch the GRADUAL transition\n5. Compare to instant reset - feels robotic!\n\nThis is why Noodlings feel more alive - their emotions\nhave inertia, just like ours.",
